IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`
IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`
IMPORT `g2-art5-charity-test`

-- ind-c-tests-art5-7: independent tests (author ind-c) of Articles 5, 6 and 7 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014.
-- Every expected value was decided from the Law before the encoding was opened: see work/ind-c/expectations.md, whose row id each assertion cites.
-- The encoding is not edited.  Assertions that fail and that ind-c believes are the encoding's fault are in ind-c-tests-disagree.l4; ambiguous ones in ind-c-tests-ambiguous.l4.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Articles 5 to 7`

-- The nine facts that Article 6(2) reads, by position in this helper only (named once, below).
GIVEN sickness IS A BOOLEAN
      regeneration IS A BOOLEAN
      civic IS A BOOLEAN
      sport IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      need IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      atLarge IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      accommodation IS A BOOLEAN
      equality IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      diversity IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-c facts` sickness regeneration civic sport need atLarge accommodation equality diversity MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS sickness
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS regeneration
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS civic
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS sport
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS need
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS atLarge
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS accommodation
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS equality
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS diversity

`ind-c no facts` MEANS `ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN h IS A MAYBE `Head of charitable purpose`
      anc IS A BOOLEAN
      pol IS A BOOLEAN
      phil IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Purpose
`ind-c purpose` h anc pol phil MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "a purpose of the ind-c test entity"
        head IS h
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS anc
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS pol
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS phil

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
      f IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`ind-c pf` p f MEANS `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH purpose IS p, facts IS f

`ind-c education` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` (JUST `the advancement of education`) FALSE FALSE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c ancillary cafe` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c profit for members` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c party politics in educational form` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` (JUST `the advancement of education`) FALSE TRUE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c candidate promotion said to be incidental` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c religion` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` (JUST `the advancement of religion`) FALSE FALSE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
`ind-c humanism` MEANS `ind-c pf` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE) `ind-c no facts`

GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-c entity` standing pfs MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Ind-C Test Entity"
        `standing on the register` IS standing
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS map (GIVEN pf YIELD pf's purpose) pfs

-- A determination of public benefit with every duty of its maker met, the benefit not confined to a section of the public.
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
      provides IS A BOOLEAN
      intends IS A BOOLEAN
      onlyIdentified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-c PB` who provides intends onlyIdentified MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS who
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS provides
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS intends
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS onlyIdentified
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A determination by the Commissioner that a section of the public benefits, subject to a fee the Commissioner had regard to (A7-04), finding public benefit.
`ind-c PB section with fee` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A7-05: the Commissioner presumed a charitable purpose (religion) to be for the public benefit.
`ind-c PB presumed` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS TRUE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A7-07: no regard to the comparison of private benefit and public disbenefit with public benefit.
`ind-c PB without the comparison` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS FALSE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A7-08: benefit to the public at large, and no regard to conditions (7(2)(b) is not engaged).
`ind-c PB public at large without regard to conditions` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- Article 5(2) permissions.
GIVEN what IS A `What a constitution expressly permits`
      who IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
      inCapacity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`ind-c constitution permitting` what who inCapacity MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH
        `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` WITH `what the constitution expressly permits` IS what, `the person permitted` IS who, `acting in that capacity` IS inCapacity)

`ind-c silent constitution` MEANS `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS EMPTY

`ind-c control` MEANS `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by`
`ind-c governor route` MEANS `any of the governors of the entity to be`
-- a Minister (5(2)(a), src:151) holding an office that is not the one the Article 1 definition names (src:26): the Minister for Health, say.
`ind-c Minister for Health` MEANS `a Minister` NOTHING

`ind-c F2 A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

-- The charity test with the favoured interpretation, the Chief Minister as the Article 1 office.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      cons IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      pb IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c meets` interp standing pfs cons pb order MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` interp (`ind-c entity` standing pfs) pfs cons `the Chief Minister` pb order

GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-c registered` MEANS `entered in the general section`
GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-c applicant` MEANS `an applicant for registration`
`ind-c good PB` MEANS `ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `ind-c Article 5 -- the charity test`

-- A5-01
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-02
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c ancillary cafe`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-03
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c profit for members`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-04
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c ancillary cafe`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-05 (and A5-09: a finding that the benefit is not to a reasonable degree is the same input)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` (`ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
-- A5-06
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c applicant` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` (`ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- A5-07
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` (`ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- A5-10 .. A5-12: activities controlled by a Minister (not the Article 1 office), a States member, a foreign equivalent, acting in that capacity
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-13 .. A5-15: the governor route
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-13 with the Article 1 office itself (the Chief Minister)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-16: a States member permitted as governor, not acting in that capacity
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-17: constitution silent (a States member who merely happens to be a governor is not a permission the text makes)
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-18: an Order under 5(3) disapplies 5(2) for the entity
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` TRUE
-- A5-19: no Order covers this entity
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-20: 5(1)(a) fails; an Order lifting 5(2) does not help
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c profit for members`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` TRUE
-- A5-21, A5-22: political purposes
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c party politics in educational form`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c candidate promotion said to be incidental`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- A5-23 (pre-committed ambiguous): no purposes.  Reading A (taken by ind-c): fails.  Reading B: vacuously meets 5(1)(a), and with public benefit found, meets.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` EMPTY `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `ind-c registered` EMPTY `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- F2.1 C (an ancillary purpose alone suffices): A5-04 then meets, by that reading's own definition
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c ancillary cafe`) `ind-c silent constitution` `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- F2.2 B (any such person is caught however the person is to act): A5-16 then fails
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.2 read as B` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c governor route` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
-- F2.3 B (only the Article 1 office): a Minister for Health is not caught; the Chief Minister is
#ASSERT `ind-c meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `ind-c good PB` FALSE

-- Which limb decides it (A5-03 fails at 5(1)(a) with the profit purpose; A5-04 at 5(1)(a) for want of a charitable purpose; A5-05 at 5(1)(b); A5-10 at 5(2))
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c profit for members`)) (LIST `ind-c education`, `ind-c profit for members`) `ind-c silent constitution` `the Chief Minister` `ind-c good PB` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one` (LIST (`ind-c profit for members`'s purpose))
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c ancillary cafe`)) (LIST `ind-c ancillary cafe`) `ind-c silent constitution` `the Chief Minister` `ind-c good PB` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(b) is not met: the entity does not provide public benefit to a reasonable degree`
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `the Chief Minister` `ind-c good PB` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(2) bars an entity that otherwise meets the charity test`
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` `the Chief Minister` `ind-c good PB` FALSE EQUALS `none: the entity meets the charity test`
-- A5-18 also: meets only by virtue of the Order
#ASSERT `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (LIST `ind-c education`) (`ind-c constitution permitting` `ind-c control` `ind-c Minister for Health` TRUE) `the Chief Minister` `ind-c good PB` TRUE

§ `ind-c Article 5(4) to (8) -- guidance`

-- A5-31: who must have regard to the guidance
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `any person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Charity Tribunal` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a registered charity` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a governor` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a governor` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the court` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- A5-32 .. A5-36: the consultation of 5(6)(a)
#ASSERT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- A5-35: no report published
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-c F2 A` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-c F2 A` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))
-- A7-09 / 5(4): the 5(4) guidance must cover public benefit
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`)
#ASSERT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`, `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit`)

§ `ind-c Article 6 -- charitable purposes`

GIVEN h IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
      f IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c head charitable` h f MEANS
    `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` (JUST h) FALSE FALSE FALSE) f

-- A6-01 .. A6-15: one purpose squarely within each of (a) to (o)
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the prevention or relief of poverty` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of education` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of religion` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of health` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the saving of lives` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of citizenship or community development` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of public participation in sport` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the promotion of religious or racial harmony` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the promotion of equality and diversity` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of environmental protection or improvement` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of animal welfare` `ind-c no facts`
-- A6-16: (p) judged analogous / no head at all
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to one of the above` `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) `ind-c no facts`
-- A6-17 .. A6-19, A6-27: the extensions of 6(2)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii), (e), with no head recorded
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c purpose` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- A6-20, A6-21: sport without / with physical skill and exertion
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of public participation in sport` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of public participation in sport` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- A6-22 .. A6-25: recreation
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c head charitable` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- A6-28: a non-theistic philosophical belief, no head recorded
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c humanism`'s purpose) `ind-c no facts`
-- A6-29, A6-30: political purposes are not charitable even under a head
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c party politics in educational form`'s purpose) `ind-c no facts`
#ASSERT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` (`ind-c candidate promotion said to be incidental`'s purpose)
-- A6-31: non-party human-rights campaigning
#ASSERT `ind-c head charitable` `the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation` `ind-c no facts`
-- A6-40: private profit
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c profit for members`'s purpose) `ind-c no facts`
-- F2.5: a philosophical belief is within (c) only on reading B
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c humanism`))
#ASSERT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c humanism`))
#ASSERT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c religion`, `ind-c education`))
-- F2.11 readings of (l): equality only
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c head charitable` `the promotion of equality and diversity` (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`ind-c purpose` (JUST `the promotion of equality and diversity`) FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))

GIVEN adds1 IS A BOOLEAN
      adds2 IS A BOOLEAN
      explains IS A BOOLEAN
      restricts IS A BOOLEAN
      alters5 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
`ind-c Regulations` adds1 adds2 explains restricts alters5 MEANS
    `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` WITH
        `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)` IS adds1
        `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)` IS adds2
        `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)` IS explains
        `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)` IS restricts
        `alters the effect of paragraph (5)` IS alters5

-- A6-32 .. A6-39
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-c Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` FALSE (`ind-c Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-c Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-c Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-c Regulations` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-c Regulations` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `ind-c Article 7 -- public benefit`

-- A7-01, A7-02: a body bound by 7(3) finds public benefit, but the entity benefits only identified natural persons
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (`ind-c PB` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) (`ind-c PB` `the Charity Tribunal` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c meets` `ind-c F2 A` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`) `ind-c silent constitution` (`ind-c PB` `the court` TRUE FALSE TRUE) FALSE
-- A7-03: a compliant determination answers with its finding
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) `ind-c good PB`
-- A7-04 (pre-committed ambiguous, reading A taken): an unduly restrictive fee is a factor; the finding stands
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c education`)) `ind-c PB section with fee`
-- A7-05: a presumption breaches 7(3)(a)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` `ind-c PB presumed` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` `ind-c PB presumed` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- F2.10, what follows from the breach: A refuses; B the finding stands; C no public benefit
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-c F2 A` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c religion`)) `ind-c PB presumed`
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c religion`)) `ind-c PB presumed`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as C` (`ind-c entity` `ind-c registered` (LIST `ind-c religion`)) `ind-c PB presumed`
-- A7-06: who is bound by 7(2) and 7(3)
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Charity Tribunal` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the court` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `any person` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- A7-07, A7-08: the regard 7(2) requires
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` `ind-c PB without the comparison`
#ASSERT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` `ind-c PB public at large without regard to conditions`


§ `Moved from ind-c-tests-disagree.l4 (POST-HOC: written after the author opened the encoding): D2 holds since the repair of G2 (R3)`


-- src:796 | (3) Any function of the Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on behalf of the Commissioner by any member of the Commissioner’s staff, except –
-- src:203 | (1) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court when determining the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit, for the purpose of Article 5(1)(b).
-- src:157 | (5) Any person, in determining whether an entity meets the charity test, must have regard to the guidance, and the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity must have regard to the guidance when performing any other of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
-- A function exercised on the Commissioner's behalf is the Commissioner's function, and the duties that attach to it go with it: otherwise authorizing staff would take a
-- determination (for example the belief of Article 27(1)(b), which staff may form under paragraph 4(3)) out of Article 7(3)(b).  The encoding answers FALSE for
-- `a member of the Commissioner's staff` (a domain.l4 constructor) in both places, so a staff determination that an entity benefiting one named person provides public benefit stands.
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a member of the Commissioner's staff` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `ind-c registered entity` `ind-c staff finding for one named person`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a member of the Commissioner's staff` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

`ind-c registered entity` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Ind-C Test Entity"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS LIST (Purpose WITH description IS "education", head IS JUST `the advancement of education`, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE)

-- A staff member, authorized under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3), finds that an entity that benefits only one named natural person provides public benefit; every other duty is met.
`ind-c staff finding for one named person` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `a member of the Commissioner's staff`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE
